  "caveats": [
    "Markov de-stabilization H_5 -> H_3 is only valid when the removed strands are DISJOINT from the closure (Markov axiom 3). The Borromean braid (s1^-1 s2)^3 uses BOTH generators of B_3 non-trivially and is Brunnian (every 2-sublink is trivial) -- so a strand cannot be removed without changing the link type. Therefore plain Markov de-stabilization does NOT give a derived H_5(fiber) -> H_3(Borromean) functor. The 5-strand fiber object and the 3-strand trace remain in different rep rings. The bridge is OPEN: a derived map requires either (a) a cabling/satellite operation (2-cabling a 3-strand pattern -> 6 strands, NOT 5), or (b) an explicit branching functor Res^{H_5}_{H_3} composed with the fiber decoration -- neither is supplied by the current framework. No fit attempted.",
    "U(1)_framing: writhe is nonzero (+2m) for the torus knots T(2,2m) and for the Hopf (sigma_1^2, w=+2), but ZERO for the Borromean baryon and the figure-eight. So a nonzero-writhe operator (e.g. a T(2,2m) color-tube operator) WOULD carry a nontrivial U(1)_framing phase q^{w.c}. This is a RAW structural observation; mapping writhe -> hypercharge Y is NOT derived and is NOT attempted. The production nucleon uses the writhe-0 Borromean, so the framing U(1) is trivial there -- consistent with the s5-so3 audit."
